WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.782
Good DAX starts with good data.

2
00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:07.405
In this lesson, you will learn to load the right tables from a workbook,

3
00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:12.359
give them clear names, and check the model, so your measures work the first time.

4
00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:13.680
Let's set the stage!

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.280
On the Home tab, choose Excel workbook, and open the chocolate sales sample.

6
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.880
The Navigator lists every table and sheet in the file.

7
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.680
Click one to preview it.

8
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.404
Some tables, like Dimension Data, are messy sheets.

9
00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:42.535
Others, like Table one to Table five, are clean tables.

10
00:00:42.535 --> 00:00:44.600
Always prefer the clean tables.

11
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.729
I tick the tables I need:

12
00:00:57.729 --> 00:01:00.357
shipments, calendar, salespeople, geography, and products.

13
00:01:00.357 --> 00:01:04.300
Then I click Transform Data, to check them first.

14
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.735
In Power Query, the names Table one, Table two, mean nothing.

15
00:01:21.735 --> 00:01:23.841
So I rename each query:

16
00:01:23.841 --> 00:01:26.369
Calendar, Sales Person, Geo, and Product.

17
00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:29.740
Clear names make DAX much easier to read.

18
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.284
I check each table:

19
00:01:56.284 --> 00:01:59.540
the data types, the headers, and a few rows of data.

20
00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.607
Then Close and Apply.

21
00:02:11.607 --> 00:02:14.620
Power BI loads each table into the model.

22
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.361
In Model view, the tables appear:

23
00:02:47.361 --> 00:02:52.260
Shipments in the middle, with Geo, Sales Person, Calendar, and Product around it.

24
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.087
Power BI has already found most relationships.

25
00:03:03.087 --> 00:03:07.780
Check them now, because every DAX measure depends on this model.

26
00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.340
Now we are ready for DAX!

